# This test is a little unexpected, but it demonstrates the behavior of nested
# evaluation's shrinking upper bound coinciding with a raising lower bound.
# More expected behavior would be to modify the second rule to `(A) -> (A)`.
A -> (A)
A -> (A)

# ===

A

# ---

(A)

# ===

(A)

# ---

((A))

# ===

((A))

# ---

(((A)))

